{"result":"{
  "metadata": {
    "id": "304840754",
    "title": "SIT Quality Gates — Thresholds &amp; Troubleshooting",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/304840754",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Adobe SFCC"
    },
    "version": 2,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "Developer-facing guide to the Digital SIT quality gate — what it checks, thresholds, and how to fix a failing check.\n\nOne-time setup (before the first SIT window)\n--------------------------------------------\n\n| Step | Action |\n| --- | --- |\n| Enable GitHub Pages | Settings → Pages, set source to GitHub Actions. Without this, the Playwright report deploy step fails on every `develop` push. |\n| Configure LHCI secrets | Add `LHCI_SERVER_BASE_URL`, `LHCI_TOKEN`, `LHCI_TARGET_URL_SIT` to GitHub Actions secrets. Without these, Lighthouse results upload to temporary public storage and trend-based blocking is inactive. |\n| Confirm MuleSoft contract source | Align with the integration team on OpenAPI spec delivery before marking the contract gate active. |\n\nWhat is the SIT gate?\n---------------------\n\nBefore any code can be promoted from Digital SIT to E2E / Pre-prod, four automated checks must all pass — enforced by GitHub branch protection. You cannot merge to `release/**` without a green `Digital SIT Gate` check. For the full job dependency graph and branch protection configuration, see [PWA CI/CD Pipeline (GitHub Actions)](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/305561601).\n\nRunning the checks locally\n--------------------------\n\n| Check | Local command | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Playwright P0 | `npm run test:sit` | Requires a running local or SIT server |\n| Lighthouse | `npm run test:lighthouse` | Set `LHCI_TARGET_URL` to your target |\n| Contract tests | `npm run test:contracts` | Currently a placeholder — see open dependency below |\n| Bundle size | `npm run bundlesize:check` | Requires a production build first: `npm run build` |\n\nWhat counts as a P0 journey?\n----------------------------\n\nP0 tests match the glob `**/*.p0.spec.{ts,js}` and live under `e2e/`. They cover the critical paths: checkout completion (guest and registered), PDP load with variant selection, cart add and remove, account login and logout. These run against Chromium only in the SIT gate. Locally, set the `SITE_ID` env var before invoking `npm run test:sit` to run a single storefront config.\n\nIf a check fails\n----------------\n\n**Playwright failure** — read the HTML report linked from the Actions summary (or published to GitHub Pages for `develop` builds). Fix the failing journey before pushing again. Do not increase `retries` in the p0 project config — retries are set to 0 intentionally. Flaky tests must be fixed, not retried away.\n\n**Lighthouse regression** — run Lighthouse locally against the SIT URL and compare to the stored baseline. A score drop > 5 points vs. the LHCI server baseline blocks. Check for new render-blocking resources or image size regressions. Thresholds: Perf ≥ 80, A11y ≥ 90, Best Practices ≥ 90.\n\n**Bundle size exceeded** — run `npm run build && npm run bundlesize:check` locally; use the bundlewatch diff to identify which chunk grew. Limits: main.js < 180 kB, vendor.js < 250 kB, main.css < 50 kB.\n\n**Contract test failure** — contact the integration team; a payload breach means either the storefront or the MuleSoft API changed its contract without alignment. Do not push workarounds.\n\nOpen dependency — contract tests\n--------------------------------\n\nMuleSoft contract tests require MuleSoft to publish OpenAPI specs to a shared repository, or expose a contract endpoint in the SIT environment. The `test:contracts` script currently exits 0 with a warning message and must be replaced with a real assertion before the contract gate is considered active. Owner: Zimmermann integration team + Accenture delivery lead.\n\nSecrets required in GitHub\n--------------------------\n\n| Secret | Purpose | Who sets it |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `LHCI_SERVER_BASE_URL` | LHCI server for trend storage | Zimmermann IT / Accenture DevOps |\n| `LHCI_TOKEN` | LHCI server auth token | Zimmermann IT / Accenture DevOps |\n| `LHCI_TARGET_URL_SIT` | SIT environment URL for Lighthouse runs | Accenture DevOps |\n\nWithout `LHCI_SERVER_BASE_URL` set, Lighthouse results upload to temporary public storage and trend-based blocking (score drop > 5 pts) is not active.\n\nWhere to find artefacts\n-----------------------\n\n| Artefact | Location |\n| --- | --- |\n| Playwright report (develop) | GitHub Pages |\n| Playwright report (PRs) | Actions → Run → Artifacts → `playwright-report` |\n| Lighthouse results | Actions → Run → Artifacts → `lighthouse-results` |\n| LHCI trend history | LHCI server URL (once configured) |\n\nBrowserStack cross-browser testing\n----------------------------------\n\nSeparate from the Digital SIT gate — runs via `qa.yml` on PRs targeting `release/**` only, after unit tests pass.\n\n**What runs:**`e2e/tests/zimm/**` — all Zimmermann Playwright tests, on Chrome, Safari, Firefox, and Edge.\n\n**Where to check results:** BrowserStack Automate dashboard, linked from the Actions job summary. Results are also synced to Zephyr via BrowserStack Test Observability once configured.\n\n**Running BrowserStack locally:**\n\nDefaultbashBROWSERSTACK\\_USERNAME=xxx BROWSERSTACK\\_ACCESS\\_KEY=yyy \\\nnpx browserstack-node-sdk playwright test e2e/tests/zimm\n\n**Secrets required:**`BROWSERSTACK_USERNAME`, `BROWSERSTACK_ACCESS_KEY`, `RETAIL_APP_HOME_SIT`, and all `E2E_*` product SKU secrets.",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "page_width": "fixed-width"
  }
}"}

