{"result":"{
  "metadata": {
    "id": "305528833",
    "title": "Guide 4: E2E Testing — Playwright &amp; Gherkin Repo Conventions",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/305528833",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Adobe SFCC"
    },
    "version": 2,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "This is the **developer-facing engineering reference** for the E2E Playwright layer in the `zimmermann-pwa` repo. For the broader BA/Tester process this plugs into (story intake → AC → Zephyr test cases → this layer → BrowserStack → defect triage), see [AI-Assisted QA — Overview & Methodology](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/277544962) and Guides 1–3.\n\nScope\n-----\n\nThis guide covers the **E2E layer** only. It is additive to — not a replacement for — the unit and component-interaction layers:\n\n| Layer | Tooling | Lives in |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Unit (pure logic) | Vitest | `*.test.ts` alongside the source |\n| Component interaction | Storybook `play` functions | `*.stories.tsx` alongside the component |\n| End-to-end user journeys | Playwright + Gherkin | `e2e/` at the repo root (this guide) |\n\nModel\n-----\n\nHuman-in-the-lead. Claude Code generates tests — a Lead QA validates them.\n\n**Rule:** never treat test generation as complete until the Lead QA has approved the `.feature` file.\n\nDefaultnoneDeveloper writes story →\n/qa-generate produces .feature file →\nLead QA validates / annotates →\nDeveloper runs /qa-generate again →\nPlaywright .spec.ts is generated →\nTest is committed\n\nDirectory layout\n----------------\n\nDefaultnonee2e/\n├── features/ # Gherkin .feature files — source of truth\n│ ├── checkout/\n│ ├── search/\n│ ├── account/\n│ ├── integrations/\n│ └── regression/ # Magento baseline parity tests\n├── fixtures/ # Test data (multi-region aware)\n│ ├── site.ts # Regional site configs (AU, US, UK, EU, ME, HK)\n│ ├── customers.ts # Guest and registered customer personas\n│ ├── products.ts # Product test data with regional pricing\n│ └── orders.ts # Order fixtures for history/confirmation tests\n├── support/\n│ ├── pages/ # Page Object Model — one file per SFCC page\n│ │ ├── basePage.ts\n│ │ ├── checkoutPage.ts\n│ │ └── productPage.ts\n│ └── helpers/\n│ └── auth.ts # Guest and registered auth helpers\n└── tests/\n└── zimm/ # Zimmermann Playwright tests (generated from .feature files)\n├── checkout/\n├── search/\n├── account/\n└── integrations/\n\nThis is a slim overrides project, not a fork of the upstream PWA Kit monorepo — there is no `e2e/tests/desktop/` or `e2e/tests/mobile/` Salesforce scaffold to preserve.\n\nWriting a feature file\n----------------------\n\n* One `.feature` file per Jira story\n* File name: `{JIRA-KEY}_{short-description}.feature`\n* Every file needs: Jira tag (`@SFCC-NNN`), area tag (`@checkout` etc.), and `@p0` if it's a critical path\n* At least one happy path and one failure/edge scenario\n* Plain English only — no selectors, no code, no technical detail\n\nGenerating tests with /qa-generate\n----------------------------------\n\nIn a Claude Code session: `/qa-generate`. The skill asks for Jira story details, drafts the `.feature` file, pauses for Lead QA validation, then generates the Playwright spec and any required Page Object additions.\n\nOnly run this on a feature branch. Never on `develop` or `main`.\n\nPage Object Model — selector priority\n-------------------------------------\n\nEnforced in code review:\n\n1. **Accessible selectors** — role + accessible name, label, visible text (`getByRole`, `getByLabelText`, `getByText`). First choice.\n2. **Semantic HTML attributes** — `getByAltText`, `getByTitle`, `getByPlaceholderText`.\n3. **`data-testid`** — last resort only, for elements with no semantic meaning.\n\nSelectors live in `e2e/support/pages/` only. Never write selectors directly in test files.\n\nMulti-region test fixtures\n--------------------------\n\nZimmermann serves 6 regions (AU, US, UK, EU, ME, HK) across **7 SFCC sites** (AU, UK, US, EU domestic, EU international, HK, ME — US confirmed as a single site, REG-005). All test data must be region-aware from day one — keyed by `SITE_ID` rather than retrofitted.\n\n> Open item: `config/sites.js` is still the OOTB Salesforce default and must be customised for the 6-site setup before regional fixtures can be wired up end-to-end — tracked on the [7.1c CI/CD & Environment Setup Checklist](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/305430530) page.\n\nDefaultbash# Default region (au)\nnpx playwright test e2e/tests/zimm\n# Specific region\nSITE\\_ID=us npx playwright test e2e/tests/zimm\n\nRunning tests locally\n---------------------\n\nDefaultbash# P0 suite only (what the Digital SIT gate runs)\nnpm run test:sit\n# All Zimmermann Playwright tests\nnpx playwright test e2e/tests/zimm\n# Single test file\nnpx playwright test e2e/tests/zimm/checkout/SFCC-000\\_guest-checkout.p0.spec.ts\n\nSet `RETAIL_APP_HOME` to your local dev server or SIT URL in `.env` at the project root.\n\nMagento baseline regression\n---------------------------\n\nFiles in `e2e/features/regression/` document expected Magento 2 behaviour.\n\nWhen a baseline test fails against SFCC: do not update the test to pass; add `# DELTA: SFCC behaviour differs — [description]`; raise with Lead QA — they classify: bug, intentional change, or platform constraint.\n\nQA annotation workflow\n----------------------\n\nWhen Lead QA annotates a correction in a `.feature` file:\n\nDefaultnone# QA ANNOTATION: Step 2 is wrong. Zimmermann checkout shows the order summary\n# BEFORE payment entry, not after. Update this scenario.\n\nResponse: update the `.feature` file to reflect the corrected behaviour, run `/qa-generate` to regenerate the Playwright spec, update the Page Object only if a new element is referenced, confirm the change.\n\nBrowserStack cross-browser runs\n-------------------------------\n\nBrowserStack runs automatically on PRs targeting `release/**` branches via `qa.yml`. Browsers tested: Chrome (OS X), Safari (OS X), Firefox (Windows), Edge (Windows). Full defect-triage flow for BrowserStack failures: see [Guide 3: BrowserStack Execution, Result Sync & Defect Triage](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/277676053).\n\nTo trigger a run manually: Actions → QA → Run workflow → select branch. Results appear in the BrowserStack Automate dashboard and Zephyr (via BrowserStack Test Observability — confirm integration with QA Lead).\n\nSecrets required\n----------------\n\n| Secret | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| `BROWSERSTACK_USERNAME` | BrowserStack account |\n| `BROWSERSTACK_ACCESS_KEY` | BrowserStack account |\n| `RETAIL_APP_HOME_SIT` | SIT storefront URL |\n| `PWA_E2E_USER_EMAIL` | Registered test account email |\n| `PWA_E2E_USER_PASSWORD` | Registered test account password |\n| `E2E_STANDARD_PRODUCT_SKU` | In-stock product for checkout tests |\n| `E2E_VARIANT_PRODUCT_SKU` | Multi-variant product for PDP tests |\n| `E2E_OOS_PRODUCT_SKU` | Out-of-stock product |\n| `E2E_SALE_PRODUCT_SKU` | Sale product for price display tests |\n| `E2E_FIXTURE_ORDER_NUMBER` | Completed order for history tests |\n\nSee the [SIT Quality Gates — Thresholds & Troubleshooting](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/304840754) page for one-time GitHub Secrets setup.\n\nWhat NOT to do\n--------------\n\n* Never write selectors directly in test files — always use Page Objects\n* Never hardcode test data in test files — always use `e2e/fixtures/`\n* Never update a baseline regression test to pass without Lead QA sign-off\n* Never generate a Playwright test before the `.feature` file has been validated\n* Never add `@skip` without a Jira ticket reference and Lead QA approval\n* Never use `page.waitForTimeout()` — use `waitForSelector` or `waitForResponse`\n* Never generate tests that only cover the happy path",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "page_width": "fixed-width"
  }
}"}

